UID:10110515-1795748400-1795834799@livemusicasheville.com
SUMMARY:COMING Wednesday Dec 23rd | The Music of A Charlie Brown Christmas
DESCRIPTION:December 23\, 2026 | Matinee: 3:00 PM | Evening: 7:00 PM Event Details and Tickets \n\n\n\nPerformed by Dr. Bill Bares and The Constellations Orchestra\n\n\n\n\nDiana Wortham Theater\n\n\n\n\n\nExperience the magic of the holidays with the iconic melodies of Vince Guaraldi that capture the nostalgic spirit of the season and where holiday tradition meets musical innovation.\n\n\nJoin URSA Asheville once again this year to experience the magic of the holidays with the iconic melodies of Vince Guaraldi that capture the nostalgic spirit of the season\, performed by The Constellations Orchestra and Dr. Bill Bares. The show will feature two sets: the first recreating the sounds of the original A Charlie Brown Christmas album and the second showcasing fresh interpretations of Bares’s arrangements of this masterpiece with the warmth and wonder of Christmas\, bringing Charlie Brown and the entire Peanuts gang to life through music. \nGet your tickets now to make this a part of your holiday celebration! Tickets range between $35 to $65; $20 for children 12 and under and for students. All proceeds from performances support URSA Asheville. \n\n\n\n  \nURSA Asheville aims to Uplift\, Renew\, and Sustain the Arts in post-Helene Asheville by fostering musical experiences that inspire\, connect\, and transform our community. Individual stars shine bright\, but when purposefully connected\, they form meaning. URSA Asheville connects talented musicians\, visionary supporters\, and passionate audiences to transform musical innovation into meaningful community experiences. ursaasheville.org
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/the-music-of-a-charlie-brown-christmas-2/2026-11-27/
LOCATION:Wortham Center for the Performing Arts
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/charlie-brown-christmas-2026-e1793630565397.jpg
GEO:35.5943091;-82.5509521
END:VEVENT
